+---
+date: 2026-04-27
+share: true
+tags:
+  - psychology
+aliases: []
+created: 2026-04-27
+---
+As someone who long suffered with Perfectionism I have come to realize the ultimate cost and more importantly that I wasn't willing to pay it anymore. This was probably one of the things that first got me interested in [[Psychology MOC|psychology]].  
+## The Cost of Perfectionism  
+  
+  
+The amount of half baked projects should be a clue. And sometimes the emotional cost wasn't even necessary. Some of my most popular writings have come from something I just "chucked over the fence." Not out of laziness but out of trying to get things completed.   
+  
+  
+You can be your own worst critic but we are often terrible at [[Self Reflection|Self Reflection]]. Our perception of our flaws may never be noticed, but worse would be our blindness to things we should actually be working on.  
+## It's Just Procrastination in Disguise  
+  
+  Perfectionism is procrastination masquerading as quality-control.  
+- From [[Readwise/Tweets/Tweets From Chris Williamson.md|Tweets From Chris Williamson]]  
+There are some things you hear that shake your reality. This was one of them for me. Because I knew that it was true.  
+## The Alternative: Progress Over Perfection  
+  
+  Think progress, not perfection.  
+- From [[Readwise/Supplementals/The Obstacle Is the Way.md|The Obstacle Is the Way]]  
+Another [[Facebookism|Facebookism]] was "[[Facebookism#Ship and Iterate|Ship and Iterate]]." There was also "Perfectionism is the Enemy of Progress" which was to say that making progress was more important.  
+  If you want to master a habit, the key is to start with repetition, not perfection. You don’t need to map out every feature of a new habit. You just need to practice it. This is the first takeaway of the 3rd Law: you just need to get your reps in.  
+- From [[Readwise/Supplementals/Atomic Habits.md|Atomic Habits]]  
+This begins to resonate even more so for [[Habits MOC|habits]]. Just because you don't lose all the weight after 1 week of workouts, doesn't mean you aren't going to get there. Focusing on the outcome metric of a long term goal can be demoralizing if the scale is too long. This is important when [[Goal Setting|goal setting]] because you want to reinforce building good habits that reinforce the long term goal.
\ No newline at end of file
