+  The test of the random sample is this: Does every name or thing in the whole group have an equal chance to be in the sample? The purely random sample is the only kind that can be examined with entire confidence by means of statistical theory, but there is one thing wrong with it. It is so difficult and expensive to obtain for many uses that sheer cost eliminates it. A more economical substitute, which is almost universally used in such fields as opinion polling and market research, is called stratified random sampling. ([171](https://readwise.io/to_kindle?action=open&asin=B00351DSX2&location=171)) %% Color: yellow %% ^824412656  
+  
+Tags: #statistics  
